WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.125
Fictional Meridian teaching case. No course example grants workplace authority . Requests and unverified claims are not approvals. Compare responsibilities and identify the appointed owner for a task that goes beyond Daniel’s role. Item 1 of 5 Executive Assistant Coordinates defined executive-support work and makes the administrative judgements actually delegated. Production, judgement and coordination reinforce each other: prepare the pack, spot an unapproved appendix and obtain the correct paper from its owner. These contributions are not ranks. A manager asks Daniel to approve a supplier exception because he has direct executive access. Here, a supplier exception means a request to depart from the normal supplier process or requirements. No approval authority for that departure has been delegated to Daniel. How can he help the request reach the appointed approver without approving it himself?
